---
import ApiKeySetup from './ApiKeySetup.astro';
interface Props { language: string; anchor: string }
const { language, anchor } = Astro.props;
---
<a id={`${anchor}-htmlcss-to-image`}></a>
<ApiKeySetup language={language} />
<a id={`generating-images-with-${anchor}`}></a>
<h2 id={`authentication-with-${anchor}`}>Authentication with {language}</h2>
<p>Use HTTP Basic authentication with your API ID as the username and API key as the password. Find both in the <a href="https://htmlcsstoimage.com/dashboard">dashboard</a>. Keep credentials in server-side configuration or environment variables.</p>
<h2 id={`${anchor}-example-code`}>{language} example code</h2>
<p>The image examples use <code>POST https://hcti.io/v1/image</code>. Recordings use <code>POST https://hcti.io/v1/recording</code> and return a recording ID and media URL. See <a href="/getting-started/recordings/">Recordings</a> for timing, actions, and output options. Both creation endpoints require <code>images:create</code>; see <a href="/getting-started/using-the-api/api-keys/">authentication and API keys</a> for scoped credentials and access errors.</p>
